The list above is the DECLARED set. The complete inventory -- around forty
artifacts per distribution once transitive dependencies are counted -- is
generated at build time by the `licenceInventory` Gradle task and ships as
THIRD-PARTY.txt in every distributed artifact, beside this file and LICENSE.

That inventory is generated from the RESOLVED runtime classpath, and each
licence is read from the artifact's own POM rather than from a list somebody
maintains by hand. Three things fail the build rather than being guessed at: an
artifact whose POM chain names no licence, a licence name that is not
allowlisted, and a copyleft artifact that is not marked as shipping unbundled.
Dual-licensed artifacts fail until this project records which licence it takes
them under, because taking whichever the POM lists first is a decision about
these obligations made by the ordering of somebody else's XML.

The allowlist, the aliases and the elections are in gradle/licences.conf, each
with its reason. gradle/libs.versions.toml remains the place a dependency is
declared, and a guard asserts nothing there is missing from this file.

docs/DECISIONS.md 10.1 records what this file claimed before a generator
existed, and for how long.
